 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2022-09-06",
   "text": "Competitive Prices Act\n This bill makes a consciously parallel pricing coordination (i.e., a tacit agreement among two or more persons to raise, lower, change, maintain, or manipulate pricing for the purchase or sale of reasonably interchangeable products or services) a prohibited form of price fixing."
  }
